INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES
('wraith-soldier', 'Wraith Soldier', 'entity', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but many are confused, angry or insane; they tend toward Unprincipled (35%) or Anarchist (40%), the rest falling evenly among the good and evil alignments', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"3D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"N/A","PB":"2D6","Spd":"48"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+12', '5D6', '1D4x10+50', 'M.D.C., P.P.E. and I.S.P. are the Wraith Brigade Entity''s (printed 23-24), and the Wraith Soldier gains another 2D6 I.S.P. and 1D4 M.D.C. per level of experience. Only energy weapons (at half damage), magic and psionics harm it; Psi-Swords do double damage and Rune Weapons normal damage. On S.D.C. worlds the M.D.C. becomes S.D.C. point for point. P.E. is not applicable. Spd 48 (36 mph/57.6 km). Horror Factor 13 is the Wraith Brigade''s; the R.C.C. prints none of its own.', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":5,"strike":2}', 'The R.C.C.''s own: +1 to save vs magic, +2 vs psionics, +4 vs Horror Factor. The Wraith Brigade''s, which the stored combat holds: five attacks per melee and +2 to strike; impervious to bullets, arrows, explosives, punches and other kinetic attacks and solid matter, to normal fire, M.D. plasma, cold, poison and disease, and needs no air. Physical skills give it no attribute bonuses, though their combat bonuses apply. Insanity on creation: 01-42 none, 43-66 one, 67-95 two, 96-00 three, rolled on the Rifts Ultimate Edition random insanity table.', 'Infantryman: Athletics (General), Climbing +5%, Cook +10%, Fishing +5% or Sewing +5%, Gambling +10%, Forced March, Military Etiquette +25%, Language: Native (English/American) 98%, W.P. Black Powder Rifle, W.P. Spear/Bayonet, W.P. one Ancient Weapon of choice, Hand to Hand: Basic (cannot be upgraded). Officer: Athletics (General), Climbing, Cook +5%, Dance +10%, History +5% (current only to the mid-19th century), Horsemanship: General +15%, Military Etiquette +30%, Language: Native (English/American) 98%, Literacy: Native Language 98%, W.P. Revolver, W.P. Sword, W.P. one Ancient Weapon of choice, Hand to Hand: Basic (cannot be upgraded). R.C.C. Related: six, at least one Wilderness or Domestic, plus one at levels 2, 4, 8 and 10. Communications: Barter and Performance only; Cowboy: any (+5%); Domestic: any (+10%); Electrical: none; Espionage: Detect Ambush, Sniper, Tracking and Wilderness Survival only (+5%); Horsemanship: none; Mechanical: none; Medical: Animal Husbandry, Brewing and Holistic Medicine only; Military: Forced March and Recognize Weapon Quality only (+10%); Physical: any, without bonuses; Pilot: Bicycling and Boats only (+10%); Pilot Related: none; Rogue: any; Science: Basic and Advanced Mathematics only (+10% for officers only); Technical: any, within reason; W.P.: any, within reason; Wilderness: any (+10%). Secondary Skills: none.', 'Runs at 36 mph (57.6 km), leaps 15 feet (4.6 m) high or across and passes through solid objects; it attacks only through psionics. Constant telepathic speech with other species, at no I.S.P., by line of sight to 200 feet (61 m). Wraith Brigade Sense: always aware of a Wraith Brigade within 1200 feet (366 m), and able to track one at 25% +5% per level for 5 minutes per level at 10 I.S.P.; a third failed roll breaks the contact until the brigade is found again. Within 200 feet (61 m) it can also sense other Entities (Haunting Entities, Wraith Children and the like), though it cannot track or count them. Being intangible it takes no bionics or cybernetics, owns only its uniform, basic gear and psionic weapons, and needs the living to carry any keepsake. Starts with no money and needs none.', 'None.', 'Master Psychic, all powers at fifth level: Ectoplasm (6 or 12), Empathy (4), Empathic Transmission (6), Mind Block (4), Presence Sense (4), See the Invisible (4), Sixth Sense (2) and Telekinesis (varies). Special Wraith Brigade powers: TK Firearm (a musket or revolver, the same either way; 2D4 M.D. per bolt and 1500 feet/457.2 m, both doubled on a ley line; 10 shots, 5 I.S.P. to recharge); Rifle Butt-Stroke (1D4 M.D. by touch, 5 I.S.P. a strike); Psi-Sword or Psi-Bayonet (3D6 M.D., 15 I.S.P., lasts 15 minutes); the Double-Quick (for one melee round, double speed for 15 I.S.P. or two extra attacks for 30 I.S.P., once per melee); the Rebel Yell or Yankee Rally (20 I.S.P., 150 feet/45.7 m; a failed save vs psionic attack means terror for 3D4 melee rounds: -4 to Perception, -6 on initiative, -4 to strike, parry and dodge, and a 01-66% chance of fleeing).', 'That of an average human male, 5 to 6 feet (1.52 to 1.8 m) tall', 'Not applicable', 'Unknown, presumably eternal', 'Mostly the Horror Forest, but reported throughout Dinosaur Swamp, the southeast and a few points north and west', 'None other than fellow Wraith Brigades; the blue-uniformed and the gray-uniformed brigades treat each other as trespassing enemies', 'Humans, D-Bees, all mortals and most large animals are trespassers; practitioners of magic and psychics are natural enemies', 'An optional R.C.C. the book leaves wholly to the Game Master, with an Infantryman and an Officer skill package (skills_note). Imported as a creature row only, not a class (Nate''s ruling D20, 2026-10-19). Experience as the Mind Melter (Rifts Ultimate Edition).', 'One of the very rare Wraith Brigade spirits with a whole personality: a Civil War soldier who remembers a 19th-century life and his own death, now displaced into Rifts Earth with that era''s education. Many are driven mad and attack anything; others seek answers or join adventurers as guides and scouts. Value: none. Its pools, powers, habitat, allies and enemies are the Wraith Brigade Entity''s (printed 23-24), which the R.C.C. extends.', 'Rifts World Book 27: Adventures in Dinosaur Swamp p.23-26'),
('alien-rex', 'Alien Rex', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal predator, considered Miscreant or Diabolic', '{"IQ":"1D4+6","ME":"1D6+6","MA":"1D6+6","PS":"1D6+25","PP":"1D6+16","PE":"1D6+16","PB":"1D6+4","Spd":"2D6+32"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6x10+60', '2D6', NULL, 'Mega-Damage by location: Head 175; Neck 110; Large Eyes (2) 12 each*; Small Eyes (2) 7 each*; Forearms (2) 75 each; Clawed Hands (2) 25 each*; Legs (2) 130 each; Tail 100; Main Body 6D6x10+60. * a Called Shot at -6 to strike. Supernatural P.S. and P.E. I.Q. is high animal intelligence. On S.D.C. worlds: 2D6x10+66 S.D.C., Hit Points equal to P.E. x10, A.R. 11.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":2,"strike":2,"dodge":2,"roll":2,"perception":1}', '+3 to strike with the bite (the stored +2 is claws and tail), +7 to save vs Horror Factor, +2 to save vs poison. All in addition to possible attribute bonuses.', 'Track by scent 65%; track a blood scent 85% up to two miles (3.2 km); Swim 30%; Prowl 42%.', 'Can sustain its usual top speed of 28 mph (45 km) for as long as 20 minutes. A leap clears 10 feet (3 m) of height and 15 feet (4.6 m) of distance, used to pounce on prey and to clear obstacles at speed. Two pairs of side-set eyes see 180 degrees to the side and rear, but it must turn its head to see what is straight ahead. A stiff opposable thumb lets it use crude tools such as a branch or a rock, though never modern weapons. Heals 4D6 M.D. per 24 hours.', 'None.', 'None.', '15-19 feet (4.6 to 5.8 m) tall, the tail another 8-12 feet (2.4 to 3.6 m); forearm reach about 6 feet (1.8 m)', '2-3 tons', '25-35 years', 'Forests and marshy lowlands throughout Dinosaur Swamp', 'None other than a mate and its own kind; often hunts in pairs, threes or fours, and groups of six or seven have been reported', 'Other large predators, including the Razorback Rhinoceros, T-Rex and Allosaurus; preys mainly on large animals, humans included', 'None; animal.', 'A theropod from another world, come through the Florida Rifts: smaller, faster and smarter than the T-Rex, with long grasping arms ending in sickle claws. Small packs herd prey toward one another; juveniles hunt alone. Value: Simvan and Psi-Stalkers may ride one but struggle to control adults; the Splugorth pay 1,000-2,000 for a young one and 4,000-6,000 for an adult for the arena.', 'Rifts World Book 27: Adventures in Dinosaur Swamp p.26-28'),
('carnosuchid', 'Carnosuchid', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal predator, considered Miscreant or Diabolic', '{"IQ":"1D4+1","ME":"1D6+2","MA":"1D6","PS":"2D6+18","PP":"2D6+10","PE":"1D6+22","PB":"1D4+4","Spd":"2D6+16 min 18"}', NULL, NULL, '4D6x10', '3D6', NULL, 'Mega-Damage by location: Head 75; Tail 35; Neck 100; Limbs (4) 60 each; Main Body 4D6x10. Supernatural P.S. and P.E. I.Q. is low animal intelligence. Minimum speed 18 (14 mph/22.4 km); most have 24 (18 mph/28.8 km), in short spurts on land. On S.D.C. worlds: 5D6x10 S.D.C., Hit Points twice the P.E., A.R. 12.', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":4,"strike":1,"dodge":1,"roll":4}', '+3 to strike with the jaws (the stored +1 is claws and tail), +3 to save vs Horror Factor, +3 vs poisons; all but those two saves are doubled underwater. Sprint Attack: in the first melee round of a fight, +4 on initiative, +2 to strike and one extra attack, after which it must rest 2D6 minutes out of combat before sprinting again. All in addition to possible attribute bonuses.', 'Track by scent 55%; track a blood scent 75% up to one mile (1.6 km), double underwater; Swim 90%.', 'Holds its breath one minute per P.E. point and sees well in dim light and murky water. Runs at top speed for one minute at most, but swims at top speed for one minute per P.E. point. Digs three cubic feet (0.28 cubic m) per melee round. Plays dead when attacked or afraid, then lunges or walks away. Bite and Thrash: after a successful bite the victim must dodge again against the unmodified roll or be locked in the jaws and thrashed for 3D6+6 M.D. per attack (2D6 S.D.C. to the wearer for every 5 M.D. to M.D.C. armor), with half his attacks, -6 to strike, parry and dodge and -25% to skills; casting or psionics first needs a save vs Horror Factor 13 and a spell takes twice as long. Breaking free takes a dodge against the original bite roll and flings the victim 15 feet (4.57 m) for 1D4 M.D., 01-50% stunned for 2D4 melee rounds.', 'None.', 'None.', '8-9 feet (2.4 to 2.7 m) long from snout to tail tip, 3 feet (0.91 m) tall at the shoulder', '450-550 lbs (202.5 to 247.5 kg)', '50-60 years', 'The Georgian Piedmont and the creeks and streams of the Horror Forest, and anywhere in the southeast (South Carolina, Georgia, Florida, Louisiana, Mississippi); in hot summers some swim up the Mississippi and its southern tributaries', 'None but a mate, for the two-month spring mating season; they seldom attack their own kind and are sometimes found in groups of 3D6', 'Other predators, especially fast dinosaurs, pack hunters, the Sarcosuchus and the Spinosaurus', 'None; animal.', 'A crocodile-like Triassic cousin of the dinosaurs whose serrated teeth are rooted deep and bound by ligaments, so it can hold and shake prey that would tear free of other jaws. A solitary scavenger and mid-level predator that marks its ground with musk and often lairs near villages and waterways. Value: an intact hide fetches 1000-2000 credits and makes light or medium M.D. armor (21 M.D.C. a conventional suit, 4D6+28 made by an Eco-Wizard); Eco-Wizards pay up to 1500 credits a head for the tooth ligaments.', 'Rifts World Book 27: Adventures in Dinosaur Swamp p.28-29'),
('devil-eel', 'Devil Eel', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal predator, considered Miscreant or Diabolic', '{"IQ":"1D4+3","ME":"1D6+4","MA":"1D6+2","PS":"1D6+16","PP":"1D6+16","PE":"1D6+18","PB":"1D6","Spd":"1D6+12"}', NULL, NULL, '3D6x10+PE', '2D6', NULL, 'Main Body 3D6x10 plus the P.E. number; each leg 12 (a Called Shot at -6); the divided tail 35. Supernatural P.S. and P.E. I.Q. is medium animal intelligence. Spd is slithering on dry land; half that in trees and triple swimming. On S.D.C. worlds: 2D6x10 S.D.C., 2D4x10+32 Hit Points, A.R. 14.', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":8,"initiative":2,"strike":2,"dodge":2,"roll":2}', 'Six attacks per melee when only biting, eight with claws, or claws and bites. +3 to strike with bites (the stored +2 is claws and tail); initiative doubled when attacking from a tree above or murky water; +4 to dodge and roll with impact underwater; +5 to save vs Horror Factor, +2 vs poison. Horror Factor is 13 for one or two, 15 for three or more. All in addition to possible attribute bonuses.', 'Track a blood scent 70% up to one mile (1.6 km) on land, twice the distance and +20% underwater; Swim 90%.', 'Has gills and lungs: breathes underwater indefinitely and lasts nine weeks on dry land before weakening (Spd, attacks and bonuses halved), dying of dehydration eight weeks after that. Good hearing, infrared vision and a polarizing second eyelid; sees in the murkiest water; fresh or salt water to 1000 feet (305 m). Burrows in mud, 10 feet (3 m) per melee round. In hard times it hibernates 1D4+2 weeks and seems dead. Regenerates 1D6 M.D. per hour; a lost leg or tongue grows back in seven days, a lost eye or section of tail in two weeks. A prehensile tongue grabs small prey (resisted with a Supernatural P.S. of 16) or whips for 2D6 S.D.C.; holding its jaws or pinning it takes a Supernatural P.S. equal to its own. Constriction: an entangled victim cannot flee and is -4 to parry and dodge. Afraid of fire: it stays 3 to 4.6 m (10-15 feet) away from a torch, and 9.1 to 15.2 m (30-50 feet) away from a big campfire.', 'None.', 'None.', '7-10 feet (2.1 to 3 m) long on average; up to 16 feet (4.9 m) captured in Florida', '300-600 lbs (135 to 270 kg) on average, up to 1500 lbs (675 kg)', '35-55 years; the largest live to 100', 'Swamps and shallow murky water, also lakes, slow rivers, forests and trees throughout Dinosaur Swamp; most common in Georgia, Florida and Louisiana, occasionally in Alabama and Mississippi', 'None but a mate and its own kind; sometimes travels and hunts in groups of 1D4+1 mated pairs', 'The Razorback Rhinoceros, other predators and humans', 'None; animal.', 'Also called the Centipede Eel: a scaled serpent with six hooked, crab-like legs that hunts in water, on land and in trees, rearing like a cobra to slash or to impale and hold. Neenok saw a kinship with the Devilsaurus in its three-fingered tongue and hooked claws. A mostly nocturnal glutton that raids camps for meat and the injured. Value: none; its meat can be eaten, though it is greasy.', 'Rifts World Book 27: Adventures in Dinosaur Swamp p.29-32'),
('devilsaurus', 'Devilsaurus', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic', '{"IQ":"1D4+9","ME":"1D6+11","MA":"1D6+5","PS":"1D6+32","PP":"1D6+15","PE":"1D6+17","PB":"1D6","Spd":"2D6+21"}', NULL, NULL, '5D6x10+176', '5D6+PE', NULL, 'Mega-Damage by location: Head 130; Horns (3 or 4) 35 each; Neck 100; Large Eyes (4) 20 each*; Small Eyes (2) 8 each*; Tongue 40*; Forearms (2) 75 each; Clawed Hands (2) 30 each*; Legs (2) 140 each; Clawed Feet (2) 80 each; Tail 150; Main Body 5D6x10+176. * a Called Shot at -5 to strike. Supernatural P.S. and P.E. I.Q. is high animal intelligence with human-like cunning. P.P.E. is 5D6 plus the P.E. number. On S.D.C. worlds: 3D6x10+55 S.D.C., Hit Points equal to P.E. x10, A.R. 13.', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":2,"strike":2,"parry":2,"dodge":3,"roll":4,"perception":3}', 'Seven attacks per melee include the tongue and tail, or two of them may be spells. +3 to strike with bites, tongue or tail (the stored +2 is claws), +4 to entangle, +2 to disarm, +8 to save vs Horror Factor, +2 vs poison, +2 vs magic and mind control. All in addition to possible attribute bonuses.', 'Land Navigation 95%, Prowl 73%, Skin and Prepare Animal (and Humanoid) Hides 87%, Tailing 89%, track by scent 55% (+20% to follow blood), track by sight 80%, Wilderness Survival 95%, Swim 96%.', 'Can keep up a top speed of roughly 20 mph (32 km) for as long as 20 minutes; cannot leap; swims like a snake about as fast as it runs; breathes underwater indefinitely, in fresh or salt water, to one mile (1.6 km) deep. Keen day vision, good hearing, nightvision 200 feet (61 m), and its six eyes see the invisible. Speech: it learns to laugh and to say short words and phrases with understanding, about as well as a four- or five-year-old, but cannot read. The prehensile tongue reaches 6-9 feet and grabs prey or pulls it into the mouth (resisted with a Supernatural P.S. of 21); holding its jaws open takes a Supernatural P.S. of 30. The prehensile tail entangles (the victim cannot flee and is -4 to parry and dodge), pins on an 18 or higher (escape takes a Supernatural P.S. of 40) and crushes for 3D6 M.D., and it can cut and skin with precision. Quick Healing (magical, no P.P.E.): recovers 1D6 M.D. per melee round (4D6 per minute); regrowth takes 48 hours for a tongue, claw, finger or toe, 72 hours for an eye, hand, foot, horn or tail tip, and two weeks for the whole tail.', 'Each of these once a day at will without spending P.P.E.; more often from its own P.P.E., but never more than half of it; all at first level: Cleanse (6), Heavy Breathing (5), Lantern Light (1; to see or to lure prey), See Aura (6), See the Invisible (4), Sense Magic (4) and Thunder Clap (4). Its Quick Healing is also magical.', 'None.', '13-16 feet (3.9 to 4.9 m) tall; the prehensile tail another 14-20 feet (4.3 to 6.1 m); forearm reach about 6 feet (1.8 m) and tongue reach 6-9 feet (1.8 to 2.7 m)', '2-3 tons', 'Unknown; at least 40-50 years, perhaps double or triple that', 'Forests, lakes and swamp lands throughout Dinosaur Swamp, sometimes along the ocean coast and the Demon Sea; most likely in Georgia, Florida and Louisiana', 'Few other than a mate; it tolerates its own kind but they never work together; sometimes keeps company with Black Faeries, Devil Unicorns and other supernatural monsters', 'Humans are prey, playthings and enemies; the Allosaurus, T-Rex, Giant Horror Turtle, Razorback Rhinoceros and Rhino-Buffalo hate and fear it and attack it until it leaves or dies', 'None; demonic predator animal.', 'A six-eyed, horned theropod with scythe claws, a hook-bladed prehensile tail and a three-fingered tongue, smart almost to a human degree and widely taken for a demon; Horune say it spawns in the Demon Sea. It stalks and tortures prey for pleasure, sabotages weapons and vehicles before it strikes, and uses captives or technology as bait. Value: none; its meat is putrid and rots within 48 hours, and only the Splugorth capture them, for the arena.', 'Rifts World Book 27: Adventures in Dinosaur Swamp p.32-35'),
('frilled-swamp-runner', 'Frilled Swamp Runner', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Anarchist', '{"IQ":"1D4+8","ME":"1D6+10","MA":"1D6+15","PS":"1D6+10","PP":"1D6+14","PE":"1D6+17","PB":"1D6","Spd":"2D6+46"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+22', '4D6+PE', NULL, 'Mega-Damage by location: Head 50; Frilled Knives (feathers; 6-10) 3 each*; Forearms (2) 15 each*; Clawed Hands (2) 10 each*; Legs (2) 40 each; Clawed Feet (2) 15 each*; Tail 30*; Main Body 6D6+22. * a Called Shot at -5 to strike. Supernatural P.S. and P.E. I.Q. is high animal intelligence with a human child''s mentality. P.P.E. is 4D6 plus the P.E. number. On S.D.C. worlds: 3D6+20 S.D.C., Hit Points equal to P.E. +10, A.R. 9.', NULL, 9, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":2,"strike":3,"parry":1,"dodge":4,"roll":3,"perception":1,"pull_punch":4}', 'Five attacks per melee include the tail, or two of them may be spells. The +3 to strike is with bites, claws or tail; a thrown Frilled Knife is +2 to strike. +4 to disarm (to snatch food from a hand, mouth or pack, or make someone drop it), +2 to save vs Horror Factor, +3 vs poison, +1 vs magic and possession. Horror Factor 9 only because it is ugly. All in addition to possible attribute bonuses.', 'Dowsing 90%, Herding Cattle 35%, Identify Plants and Fruit 90%, Land Navigation 95%, Prowl 45%, Tailing 60%, Wilderness Survival 95%, sniff out food by scent 65% up to 3000 feet (914 m) (four times that on the wind), track by sight 50%.', 'Can keep up a top speed of about 35 mph (56 km) for two hours; a leap covers 6 feet (1.8 m) of height and 10 feet (3 m) of distance; cannot climb trees or swim. Keen day vision and good hearing. Speech: learns single words and short phrases with understanding, in a shrill voice, and is a gifted mimic; it cannot read, but may pretend to. Heals 1D6+1 M.D. per 24 hours; a lost tail, finger or toe takes a month to grow back, small Frilled Knives a week, and large ones two weeks. Frilled Knife Quills: like a porcupine it plucks one of its 1D4+6 feather-like knives (3-5 on the head, the rest on the back) to cut, pry or throw.', 'By spending its own P.P.E., all at first level: Cleanse (6), Climb (3), Concealment (6), Death Trance (1), Energy Bolt (5; fired from the hand or eyes), Light Healing (6) and Manipulate Objects (2+). Run on Water: for one P.P.E. it runs, walks and stands on water as naturally as on the ground.', 'None.', '3 to 3.5 feet (0.9 to 1 m) tall; the prehensile tail 4-6 feet (1.2 to 1.8 m) long', '45-60 lbs (20 to 27 kg)', 'Unknown; at least 30 years, perhaps double that', 'Forests, lakes and swamp lands throughout Dinosaur Swamp, sometimes along the ocean coast and the Demon Sea; most likely in Georgia, Florida and Louisiana', 'Other Frilled Swamp Runners; they sometimes run or play with Scampers, monkeys, Faerie Folk, domestic dogs, and even humanoid children and adventurers', 'Humans and most predators, especially the Raptors; they tend to avoid evil beings', 'None; animal scavenger.', 'A small, bony biped with a skeletal head, sometimes mistaken for an undead baby Raptor: an omnivore as clever and playful as a chimpanzee, and a destructive pest that raids towns like Char for garbage, eggs, small pets and food snatched from people''s hands. Clans of 2-6, never more than 10; one that adopts a family protects its children, and a clan will harass a captor for days, or follow for up to 200 miles (320 km), to free a captured member. Value: none; too destructive for pets and too tough to eat.', 'Rifts World Book 27: Adventures in Dinosaur Swamp p.37-38'),
('giant-hunter-turtle', 'Giant Hunter Turtle', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal predator, considered Miscreant or Diabolic', '{"IQ":"1D4+3","ME":"1D6+4","MA":"1D6+6","PS":"2D6+40","PP":"1D6+15","PE":"1D6+20","PB":"1D6","Spd":"1D6+18 min 19"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x100+230', '2D6', NULL, 'Mega-Damage by location: Head 120; Neck 140; Tongues (2) 20 each*; Eyes (4) 10 each*; Legs (6) 100 each; Clawed Feet (8, as printed, though the text gives it six feet) 60 each; Tail 180; Main Body: Top Shell 1D6x100+230 (stored); Main Body: Underbelly Shell 3D6x10+200. * a Called Shot at -5 to strike. Supernatural P.S. and P.E. I.Q. is low animal intelligence. Spd is on dry land, minimum 19 (14 mph/22.4 km), and 50% more swimming. On S.D.C. worlds: 3D6x10+100 S.D.C., 1D4x100 Hit Points, A.R. 18 for the top shell, 16 for the belly shell and 13 for the neck and exposed parts.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":3,"strike":2,"parry":1,"dodge":1}', 'Six attacks per melee include the tail and tongues. +3 to strike with tongue, tail or biting head (the stored +2 is claws, body rams and all else), its reach often underestimated; +9 to save vs Horror Factor, +2 vs poison, +1 vs psionic attack and possession. All in addition to possible attribute bonuses.', 'Swim 78%; Prowl 45% (underwater only).', 'Holds its breath up to 30 minutes; excellent day vision; smells blood, rot and decay a mile (1.6 km) away, triple on the wind, and has learned the smell of livestock at half that range. Two sticky prehensile tongues snare small prey, weapons or a limb and whip them into its jaws (resisted with a Supernatural P.S. of 30 or a robotic P.S. of 45), at one target or two. Its long-nailed feet dig a pit to lie in. Bio-regenerates 2D6+12 M.D. per 24 hours anywhere on the body, an eye, foot or tongue in two weeks and the tail or a leg in eight. Vulnerable: slow on dry land and fearless of men and M.D. weapons, so modern weapons and magic catch it out; it retreats to the woods or underwater when prey proves too tough.', 'None.', 'None.', 'Most commonly 8-15 feet (2.4 to 4.6 m) across and 8-12 feet (2.4 to 3.6 m) tall; the neck extends half the body length and the tail is two-thirds of it', '5-10 tons, by size', 'Unknown; could live for centuries', 'Throughout Dinosaur Swamp, most common in Georgia and Florida; in much smaller numbers in Mississippi and along the Mississippi River as far north as Tennessee', 'None; it barely tolerates its own kind and hunts and scavenges alone except when mating', 'Humans and large predators; anything that fits in its maw or threatens it is prey; pack hunters leave it alone unless it is sick or badly hurt', 'None; animal.', 'Also called the Giant Hammer Turtle (Neenok''s Ankylomonstromus): a six-legged snapping turtle from another dimension with a spiked club of a tail, which bullies predators off their kills and bulldozes into pens and camps for livestock and people; it is drawn to dumps, battlefields and fresh graves. Value: natives think killing any giant turtle a terrible curse; the meat is good, the claws and spikes serve as M.D.C. building material, and the teeth make M.D. arrows (1 M.D.), spearheads and war clubs (1D6 M.D. each); the shell turns brittle after death.', 'Rifts World Book 27: Adventures in Dinosaur Swamp p.38-40'),
('giant-petal-turtle', 'Giant Petal Turtle', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal predator, considered Anarchist or Miscreant', '{"IQ":"1D6","ME":"1D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"3D6+40","PP":"1D6+15","PE":"1D6+20","PB":"1D6","Spd":"1D6+12 min 13"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x1000', '3D6', NULL, 'Mega-Damage by location, for a typical tank-sized turtle (double all of it for true giants 100 feet/30.5 m or more across): Head 225; Neck 150 per 10 feet (3 m) of length; Eye Stalks (3) 45 each*; Mouth Sections (3) 80 each*; Legs (8) 300 each; Clawed Feet (8) 150 each; Main Body: Top Shell 1D6x1000 (stored); Main Body: Underbelly Shell 1D6x100+180. * a Called Shot at -5 to strike. Supernatural P.S. and P.E. I.Q. is low animal intelligence. Spd is on dry land, minimum 13 (8 mph/12.8 km), and 50% more swimming. On S.D.C. worlds: 3D6x10+400 S.D.C., 1D6x100 Hit Points, A.R. 19 for the top shell, 16 for the belly shell and 14 for the neck and exposed parts.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":3,"strike":1}', '+3 to strike with any biting or blunt head attack (the stored +1 is every other attack); its neck reaches twice its body length and is often underestimated. Head and neck are +4 to automatic dodge, which uses no melee action. +8 to save vs Horror Factor, +3 vs poison, +2 vs magic and possession. Horror Factor 18 for the largest and most aggressive. All in addition to possible attribute bonuses.', 'Swim 98%; Prowl 75% (underwater only).', 'Natural camouflage, since plants grow on its shell and it can pass for a small island. Digs in soft earth and mud; holds its breath up to 45 minutes; excellent vision, infrared vision and nightvision 600 feet (183 m). Three eyes on independent prehensile stalks look every way at once; the mouth opens in three petal-like sections; eight spiked legs make it impossible to budge. Survives out of water up to three weeks and may travel hundreds of miles over land. Bio-regenerates 1D6x10 M.D.C. every six hours anywhere on the body; a lost eye stalk returns in 24 hours, a foot or a section of mouth in 48, and a leg in 72. Vulnerable: fearless of men and M.D. weapons and slow on land, so hunters and predator packs can bring it down; it goes underwater to escape surface attackers. One turtle in thirty carries some intelligent being on its back, such as 1D4 Faerie Folk.', 'Each of these twice a day at will, without spending P.P.E., at second level: Create Fog (5), Dowsing (2), Ride the Waves (7) and Sense Direction Underwater (4).', 'None.', 'Most commonly 16-24 feet (4.9 to 7.3 m) across and 12-16 feet (3.6 to 4.9 m) tall; the largest are reputed to reach 100 feet (30.5 m) across and 60 feet (18.3 m) tall', '6-10 tons on average, 15-30 tons for the largest', 'Unknown; could live for centuries', 'Throughout Dinosaur Swamp, most common in Georgia and Florida; in much smaller numbers in Mississippi and along the Mississippi River as far north as Tennessee', 'None, not even its own kind', 'Humans and pack predators; anything that fits in its maw or threatens it is prey', 'None; animal.', 'Also called the Island Turtle and the Giant Horror Turtle (Neenok''s Chelonmaximus Rex): a tank-sized, eight-legged turtle from another dimension whose shell grows plants and sometimes hosts birds and Faerie Folk, and whose neck stretches twice its body length. A scavenger and ambush predator of fish, birds and crocodilians that takes people in boats when hungry, and ignores them when fed; barbarians sometimes ride a sated one through dangerous water. Value: natives think killing any giant turtle a terrible curse; the meat is delicious, the blubber gives lantern oil, the top shell makes a hut with a third of the turtle''s M.D.C., and each of its 24 belly plates keeps 3D6+6 M.D.C.', 'Rifts World Book 27: Adventures in Dinosaur Swamp p.40-42'),
('giant-swamp-turtle', 'Giant Swamp Turtle', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal predator, considered Anarchist or Miscreant', '{"IQ":"1D4+2","ME":"1D6+1","MA":"1D6","PS":"1D6+15","PP":"1D6+12","PE":"1D6+20","PB":"1D6","Spd":"1D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, '4D6x10+40', '1D6', NULL, 'Mega-Damage by location: Head 75; Tail 15; Neck 75; Limbs (4 webbed feet) 40 each; Main Body 4D6x10+40. Supernatural P.S. and P.E. I.Q. is low animal intelligence. Spd 1D6+6 is on dry land, which it seldom visits; it swims at 1D4+16 (about 15 mph/24 km), with a burst of twice that for one melee round. On S.D.C. worlds: 3D6x10 S.D.C., Hit Points twice the P.E., A.R. 13 (soft shell); the bite does 3D6 S.D.C. and the claws 2D4.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":3,"strike":2,"parry":1,"dodge":3,"roll":4}', 'Every bonus applies only underwater: +2 to strike, +1 to parry, +3 to dodge, +4 to roll with impact, +4 to save vs Horror Factor and +2 vs poisons. All in addition to possible attribute bonuses.', 'Tracks prey by sight and movement in the water 70% up to half a mile (0.8 km); Swim 98%.', 'Good sense of smell; holds its breath two minutes per P.E. point and sees well in dim light and murky water. Two tentacle-like feelers on its head sense currents and nearby movement in the dark, and with its spiny back fins catching weeds it passes for floating debris. Fights to the death when cornered, or until it can escape. Drowning grip: once it has a firm hold it dives, shaking and bashing the victim for 1D6 M.D. per melee attack (1D4 S.D.C. to the wearer for every 5 M.D. to environmental armor); a typical air-breathing victim drowns within 1D4+2 minutes. The held victim has half his attacks, -6 to strike, parry and dodge and -25% to skills, and cannot cast without a helmet that lets him speak; pulling free takes a dodge against the original bite roll, and leaves him 01-50% stunned for 1D4 melee rounds.', 'None.', 'None.', '5-7 feet (1.5 to 2.1 m) long, 3-4 feet (0.9 to 1.2 m) wide', '400 to 1000 lbs (180 to 450 kg)', '60-80 years', 'Mostly the swamps and lakes of Dinosaur Swamp; fewer in Louisiana, Alabama and Mississippi', 'None; a solitary hunter', 'Other predators, especially aquatic dinosaurs such as the Carnosuchid, Sarcosuchus and Spinosaurus', 'None; animal.', 'An alien cousin of the snapping turtle the size of a canoe: a minor Mega-Damage ambush predator whose toothless, bone-rimmed jaws cut M.D. flesh, and which drags large prey, people included, under to drown. Value: none; the meat is foul and makes humans violently sick.', 'Rifts World Book 27: Adventures in Dinosaur Swamp p.42-44'),
('gruesome-tarbid', 'Gruesome Tarbid', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal predator, considered Miscreant or Diabolic', '{"IQ":"1D6+3","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"2D6","PS":"35+2D6","PP":"20+1D6","PE":"30+2D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"32+2D6 min 34"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x100+50', '6D6', NULL, 'Mega-Damage by location: Head 50*; Mandibles 45**; Legs (8) 110 each; Main Body 1D4x100+50. * a Called Shot at -3; ** a Called Shot at -6. Supernatural P.S. and P.E. I.Q. is medium animal intelligence. Minimum speed 34 (26 mph/41.6 km); most have 38 (29 mph/46.4 km). In S.D.C. environments: 1D4x100 S.D.C., Hit Points three times the P.E., A.R. 13.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":6,"strike":1,"parry":3,"dodge":3,"roll":3}', 'The +3 dodge is an automatic dodge, which uses no melee attack. +2 to save vs magic, +2 vs psionics, +6 vs poison, +12 vs Horror Factor; absolutely fearless. All in addition to possible attribute bonuses.', NULL, 'Impervious to disease. Walks, runs and climbs on walls, trees, rock faces and upside down; only smooth, glassy surfaces slow it, to half speed. Its sensitive body hairs feel the slightest air movement, so it is almost impossible to sneak up on and dodges automatically. Nightvision 150 feet (45.7 m), infrared vision 300 feet (91.4 m). Its venom and web are magical in nature (see the attacks), though it casts no spells.', 'None as spells; its venom is anti-magic and its web equals the fourth-level Invocation Magic Net, at no P.P.E. cost.', 'None.', '20 feet (6.1 m) long, 18 feet (5.4 m) tall', '1800 lbs (810 kg)', '11 years', 'Throughout the Horror Forest, in the largest numbers on its northern edge near the Appalachian Mountains', 'None; even other Gruesome Tarbids are food', 'Everything; just about anything that moves is food', 'None; animal.', 'A giant, jet-black, hair-covered spider of the Horror Forest that hunts dinosaurs with paralytic, anti-magic venom and magical webbing; New Lazlo scholars wonder whether it is a primitive cousin of Central America''s Death Weaver Spiders. Cannibalistic, and fewer than 2% of young reach adulthood; a brooding female may take a whole barbarian village to house her eggs and feed her hatchlings. Value: the venom fetches as much as 2000 credits a quart (liter) from Eco-Wizards and other barbarians, who often use it on tribal rivals.', 'Rifts World Book 27: Adventures in Dinosaur Swamp p.44-45');
